  "_chrome_versions_comment": "Deliberately a single entry, matching the ONE Chromium version these patches are actually verified against (see CHROMIUM_VERSION in scripts/setup.sh / scripts/build_linux.sh / scripts/build_macos.sh / scripts/build_windows.bat). Real Chrome major/build/patch version is visible to sites via more than navigator.userAgent (Client Hights getHighEntropyValues, feature-detection of version-gated JS APIs, internal error message text, etc.) — claiming a version that doesn't match what's actually compiled is a bigger, more mechanically detectable tell than the UA string alone suggests. Do NOT add more entries here to fake version diversity; that requires actually building and pinning additional Chromium versions (see the packaging discussion — this list must always match reality, one weighted entry per Chromium build you've actually produced).",
  "user_agent_templates": {
    "Windows": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/{full_version} Safari/537.36",
